# Verifying a change

A change is done when it has been checked against real output, not when the code looks right.

- Run the CI checks (`uv sync --locked`, `ruff check`, `ruff format --check`, and
  `pytest tests --cov-fail-under=<minimum in test.yml>`) and report failures as they are.
- Diagram or template changes: run `uv run codeatlas --source . --diagrams-only -o <dir>`,
  serve the folder with `python3 -m http.server 8765 --bind 127.0.0.1`, and look at each
  changed page in a browser. The validator checks known rules; only Mermaid itself shows
  whether a diagram renders. For layout or noise problems, also try a larger real codebase.
- Prompt or section changes need a paid run. Ask before running anything that calls the
  Anthropic or OpenAI APIs, and say which model and roughly what it costs (the FastAPI
  package costs about $0.26 with the default Sonnet model; see `docs/architecture.md`).
- Check the claims in generated sections against the source code. A section that reads well
  can still describe an API that does not exist.
- Treat claims from other agents and tools, including your own earlier summaries, as
  unverified until checked.
- When behavior or a flag changes, update `README.md`, `docs/architecture.md`, or
  `CONTRIBUTING.md` in the same change.
- In the summary, say what was verified and how, and what was not.
